8. Password Policy Validation Engine

1. Problem Statement
Validate sample passwords against minimum length, uppercase, lowercase, digit, special-character, repeated-character
, and prohibited-substring rules. Report each failed rule.

2. Objectives
•	Check password length and character categories.
•	Detect repeated consecutive characters.
•	Report all failed policy conditions.

3. Assumptions
•	Minimum length is 8 characters.
•	Password must contain uppercase, lowercase, digit, and one of !, @, #, $.
•	Three identical consecutive characters are prohibited.
•	The substring 'password' is prohibited regardless of letter case.

4. Algorithm
1. Read a sample password.
2. Check each required condition.
3. Check for three consecutive identical characters.
4. Check prohibited substring case-insensitively.
5. Print failures or valid status.

5. Flowchart
       (START)
          |
     Enter Password
          |
    Check Password
          |
   Check Repeated Letters
          |
   Check Prohibited Words
          |
     Find Errors
          |
   Print Password Status
          |
        (STOP)

6. Pseudocode
BEGIN
INPUT material, labour, machine cost
INPUT wastage percentage and selling price
CALCULATE total production cost including wastage
CALCULATE profit
IF profit >= target, DISPLAY target achieved
ELSE DISPLAY target not achieved
DISPLAY cost and profit
END

7. Python Source Code
m = float(input("Material cost: "))
l = float(input("Labour cost: "))
mc = float(input("Machine cost: "))
w = float(input("Wastage percentage: "))
s = float(input("Selling price: "))
cost = (m + l + mc) * (1 + w / 100)
profit = s - cost
print("Total Cost:", round(cost, 2))
print("Profit:", round(profit, 2))
print("Target Achieved" if profit >= 500 else "Target Not Achieved")

